***TIME_AND_RESOLUTION***
1.d0            Total time [Myr]
100              Write checkpoints [-1=false, othwerise indicate the timestep frequency]
-1              Resume from checkpoint [to activate it, indicate a positive integer]
1.d-5           Output times 1D [Myr]
1.d-3           Output times 2D and 3D (Paraview) [Myr]
15              Number of the thermal cells in the crust, in the angular direction (nangt)
15              Number of the thermal cells in the radial direction (nrt)
50              Number of core shells (ncore, just for microphysical calculations)
***MAGNETIC FIELD***
true           Magnetic field evolution [true/false]
100.              Poloidal normalization [bpol_init]
1000.              Toroidal normalization [btor_init]
***TEMPERATURE***
true           Temperature evolution [true/false]
Gudm           Envelope model (Gudm, Iron_PPP15, Accr_mag, Accr, Iron_PMG09, Iron_PY01, Iron_DV13)
1.d2            Initial temperature [10^8 K]
***STRUCTURE***
SLy4mu          EoS [Just a shell: "simple". From CompOSE: SLy4mu, SLy2mu, SkMpmu, Skamu, SKbmu, CMF2mu, CMF6mu]
1.36e35         Central pressure [cgs]
1e28            Crust/envelope pressure [cgs]
realist         fh and eta profiles ("realist" needs an EoS;"uniform","Vigan21","Clara22")
true            Use relativistic grid [true/false]
1d0             Impurity parameter in the crust (Qimp)
1d2             Impurity parameter in the pasta phase (Qpasta)
***SUPERFLUIDITY*** (needs an EoS)
SFB             SF n crust [0=deactivate] [advice: SFB] (see superfluid.f90)
TToa            SF n core [0=deactivate] [advice: TToa] (see superfluid.f90)
CCDKp           SF p core [0=deactivate] [advice: CCDKp] (see superfluid.f90)
***NUMERICAL METHODS FOR MAGNETIC FIELDS***
RK4             Time advance method ("Eul","RK2","RK3","RK4")
0.1d0           Courant pre-factor in adaptive timestep (set=0 to fix timestep to dtb0)
1d-8            Minimum magnetic timestep [Myr] (dtb0)
Center          Scheme for Etor computation ["Center" -advised- or "Upwind"]
***COOLING TIMESTEP***
1d-7            Minimum cooling timestep [Myr] (min_dt_cooling) [1d-7]
1d-3            Maximum cooling timestep [Myr] (max_dt_cooling) [1d-3]
0.1d0           Timestep/time in cooling advance (max_dt_cooling) [0.1]
**********************
